WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.500
Italy is a boot-shaped Mediterranean peninsula, birthplace of the Roman Empire and the Renaissance.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:11.000
In Rome, the historic Colosseum amphitheater spans 189 meters in length, holding 50,000 spectators.

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:17.000
Monte Bianco on the northwestern alpine border reaches 4,808 meters as the highest summit in Italy.

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:23.000
Standard Italian descends from the literary Tuscan dialect pioneered by Dante Alighieri.

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:29.000
Italian cuisine is world-renowned for handmade pasta, Neapolitan wood-fired pizza, and olive oil.

